## 🎨 Design Principles

### Code Quality
- **Type Safety**: Comprehensive TypeScript coverage, SQLx compile-time checks
- **Performance**: Async/await throughout, optimized bundle splitting
- **Modularity**: Clean separation of concerns, reusable components
- **Error Handling**: Robust error boundaries and graceful degradation

### Responsive Design
- **Mobile-First**: DIN A4 proportional scaling across devices
- **Touch Optimization**: 44px minimum touch targets, gesture-friendly
- **Fluid Typography**: CSS clamp() for responsive scaling
- **Progressive Enhancement**: Works without JavaScript, enhanced with it

### Collaboration
- **CRDT-Based**: Conflict-free replicated data types via Yjs
- **Real-time Sync**: WebSocket server with automatic reconnection
- **Offline Support**: IndexedDB persistence with background sync
- **Presence Indicators**: Live cursors and user awareness

## 🔧 Development Guidelines

### Rust Backend Development
```rust
// Always use async/await with proper error handling
pub async fn create_script(pool: &PgPool, title: &str, user_id: Uuid) -> Result<Script> {
    sqlx::query_as!(
        Script,
        "INSERT INTO scripts (id, title, created_by) VALUES ($1, $2, $3) RETURNING *",
        Uuid::new_v4(),
        title,
        user_id
    )
    .fetch_one(pool)
    .await
    .map_err(|e| AppError::Internal(Error::msg(e.to_string())))
}

// Use timeouts for all I/O operations
async fn with_timeout<T>(future: impl Future<Output = T>) -> Result<T> {
    timeout(Duration::from_secs(5), future)
        .await
        .map_err(|_| AppError::Internal(Error::msg("Operation timed out")))
}
```

### React Frontend Development
```tsx
// Use custom hooks for complex logic
const useEditorCore = ({ scriptId, user, token }: EditorCoreProps) => {
  const [editor, setEditor] = useState<Editor | null>(null);
  const [connectionStatus, setConnectionStatus] = useState<ConnectionStatus>('connecting');
  
  // Memoize expensive operations
  const provider = useMemo(() => 
    new WebsocketProvider(wsUrl, scriptId, ydoc), 
    [wsUrl, scriptId]
  );
  
  return { editor, connectionStatus, provider };
};

// Proper TypeScript interfaces
interface EditorProps {
  scriptId: string;
  initialTitle?: string;
  onNavigateBack: () => void;
}
```

### CSS Architecture
```css
/* Use CSS custom properties for consistency */
:root {
  --page-width: clamp(300px, 85vw, 21cm);
  --page-height: calc(var(--page-width) * 1.414);
  --font-size-base: clamp(15px, 2.2vw, 16px);
  --color-primary: #2563eb;
  --color-text: #1f2937;
}

/* Mobile-first responsive design */
.editor-container {
  width: var(--page-width);
  height: var(--page-height);
  margin: 0 auto;
}

@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .toolbar {
    position: fixed;
    bottom: 0;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
  }
}
```

## 🚀 Development Workflow

### Local Development
```bash
# Start with hot reload (instant changes)
./deploy_local.sh --hot-reload

# Build specific components
./deploy_local.sh frontend --no-cache
./deploy_local.sh backend --reset-db

# URLs:
# Frontend: http://192.168.2.111:8444 (hot reload)
# Backend: http://192.168.2.111:3001/api
# Database: postgresql://localhost:5432/pessoa_db
```

### Production Deployment
```bash
# Deploy to Hetzner production
./deploy_hetzner.sh

# URLs:
# Production: https://pessoa.theater
# Backend: https://pessoa.theater/api
# Admin: http://pessoa.theater:5050
```

## 📊 Database Schema

### Core Tables
- **users**: Authentication and user management
- **scripts**: Script metadata and sharing settings
- **blocks**: Script content blocks with ordering
- **edits**: Historical changes for audit trail
- **yjs_document_updates**: Real-time collaboration data
- **script_layouts**: Visual layout configurations

### Key Relationships
```sql
scripts (1) -> (n) blocks
scripts (1) -> (n) script_shares
users (1) -> (n) scripts (created_by)
blocks (1) -> (n) edits
```

